{
  "case_id": "2007-07-219",
  "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Exxon Shipping Company (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When the Exxon Valdez ran aground in Prince William Sound on March 24, 1989, the resulting spill of 11 million gallons of oil was one of the worst environmental tragedies in U.S. maritime history. The only remaining aspect -- the only aspect of the litigation over the Valdez disaster that is before the Court today concerns almost entirely lost revenues by the commercial fishing industry. Exxon long ago paid $400 million in compensation for that lost revenue. At issue here is whether an additional warrant to the commercial fishing class of $2.5 billion dollars in punitive damages is permissible under Federal Maritime Law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Dellinger, how was that rule settled? You go in that story and The Amiable Nancy, but no one even raised the question of punitive or exemplary damages in those cases. So what is the long-settled line of decisions of this Court in maritime law that you are relying on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the shipowner is, I suppose, the owner of Exxon or the hundreds of thousands of shareholders, right? So you have to have a shareholder driving the boat before you can assess liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I right, Mr. Dellinger, that in the railroad case the court was dealing with the concept of respondeat superior? It didn't make any distinction between regular employees and managerial employees, and, indeed, it was not dealing with a managerial employee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In some punitive-damages cases, the liability attaches because the person has hired someone who is obviously incompetent. Supposing that the -- a crew member was -- an obviously incompetent crew member was hired by the captain of the ship. Would that be sufficient to justify punitive damages?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dellinger (Exxon)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court itself has never affirmed an award of punitive damages under maritime law. It has never held that punitive damages are available for unintentional conduct in maritime law. It has never held that they were available for oil spills."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My only question is this: Assume that there will be punitive damages applicable to Exxon under maritime law in in case. We have read in the briefs about the limits that should be imposed on these punitive damages. And those are from our due-process cases. If we are deciding this case as a matter of our authority to determine Federal maritime law, are there factors that we should include in a punitive-damages framework that do not -- that do not appear in our due-process cases? And, if so, what are those factors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, it is our submission that it is perfectly appropriate to expose the corporation to punitive damages based on the reckless acts of such an individual."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are about 20 vessels like the Valdez."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Exxon",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Exxon itself recognized that you have to draw the line somewhere."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do any of those cases say the managerial agent is liable if he violated express instructions from an employer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What about -- what about looking to the Clean Water Act? And I wanted to ask you this question about the Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: That's right, Justice Ginsburg. And at page 103 of the joint appendix, the district court ruled on that motion and held that TAPAA was the statute that was controlling with respect to spills of trans-Alaska oil and that the savings clause of TAPAA expressly preserved our ability to seek punitive damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Exxon",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, I think Exxon's primary argument on deterrence grounds is that we've paid $3.4 billion out of our pocket already as a result of this spill, and that's a lot of money. The reality is, once they get their tax credit and insurance benefits for that money, the number is really under 2 billion. But it's still a lot of money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "of putting a drunken master in charge of a supertanker was a potential for disaster and incalculably raised the chances of a disaster and a catastrophic spill occurring. Knowing all this; knowing what could happen; knowing that the industry did not have sufficient cleanup equipment to contain a big spill; knowing that tens of thousands of Alaskans that depended on Exxon taking proactive action, the kind of action that Congress had demanded in passing the TAPAA; Exxon nonetheless left Captain Hazelwood in command over a three-year span."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "are there other cases against Exxon seeking compensation and punitive damages based on this oil spill that are still awaiting trial or decision? Or is this it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By definition, Justice Ginsburg, this is a mandatory punitive class, so this is the one and only time Exxon will face the respect of punitive damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me begin by noting that it's -- I do not think the Court will find in the record that Exxon said this was expected and approved the -- you can look at that excerpt on the DVD and see for yourself what was -- what was meant by that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At the end of the day what the Ninth Circuit held was that Exxon was liable -- could be liable for 2.5 billion, simply because against its policies, Hazelwood left the deck."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What was substantial there was 1 million dollars. The compensatories here were 400 or 500 times the -- what the Ninth Circuit found -- 504 million dollars."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here we're at 500 times what was considered substantial in State Farm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-07-219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06abfc191925-0004-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:38 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
